{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.ClassicalLimitStpart","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.ClassicalLimitStpart","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.canonical","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/ClassicalLimitStpart.lean#L70-L95","doc":"**Trivial-zero skeleton.**  All three functions are constant zero,\nso `cl_via_stpart_holds` reduces to `0 = 0` and closes by `rfl`.\nIt encodes none of the classical-limit / standard-part content.\n\n**A `def`, not an `instance`, since 2026-08-24.**  It takes no\nparameters, so as an `instance` it was *the* global\n`ClassicalLimitStpart`: `classical_limit_eq_stpart`, labelled a\n\"Downstream conditional theorem (AGENTS.md §3b-cond)\", had nothing\nleft to be conditional on and asserted `0 = 0` for every `q ≥ 1`.\n\nNote also what the class docstring above says a concrete instance\nshould look like: it *\"discharges `cl_via_stpart_holds` with\n`sorry` (the conjecture)\"*.  This one discharges it with `rfl`.\nThose are different states — a `sorry` is an admitted conjecture\nthat `#print axioms` reports and the vacuity audit can find; a\n`rfl` over constant-zero data reports clean while proving nothing.\nThe class docstring describes a declaration this file does not\ncontain.\n\nCallers name it: `letI := canonical`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.classical_limit_eq_stpart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.classical_limit_eq_stpart","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/ClassicalLimitStpart.lean#L60-L68","doc":"**Downstream conditional theorem (AGENTS.md §3b-cond).**\nConditional on `[ClassicalLimitStpart]`, the classical-limit\nvalue at any q ≥ 1 is the standard-part of the q-evaluation\nat q = 1 + ε.  Fully verified by Lean once an instance is\nfixed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.ClassicalLimitStpart.cl_via_stpart_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.ClassicalLimitStpart.cl_via_stpart_holds","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/ClassicalLimitStpart.lean#L56-L56","doc":"**Conjectural identification.**  The classical limit equals\nthe standard part of the q-evaluation at q = 1 + ε.  A\nconcrete instance discharges this by `sorry` (the conjecture);\ndownstream theorems condition on it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.ClassicalLimitStpart.q_quantity_at","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.ClassicalLimitStpart.q_quantity_at","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/ClassicalLimitStpart.lean#L51-L51","doc":"The q-deformed quantity itself, evaluated at q = 1 + ε\n(here represented as a function ε ↦ value(1 + ε)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.ClassicalLimitStpart.st_part","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.ClassicalLimitStpart.st_part","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/ClassicalLimitStpart.lean#L48-L48","doc":"Standard-part operator (surrogate for the surreal-st map). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.ClassicalLimitStpart.cl_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.ClassicalLimitStpart.cl_value","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/ClassicalLimitStpart.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Classical-limit value of a q-deformed real-valued quantity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.ClassicalLimitStpart.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.ClassicalLimitStpart.mk","kind":"ctor","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/ClassicalLimitStpart.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.ClassicalLimitStpart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.ClassicalLimitStpart","kind":"class","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/ClassicalLimitStpart.lean#L33-L58","doc":"**Conjecture class.**  An instance asserts the existence of:\n* a classical-limit functor `cl_value : ℝ → ℝ` taking a\n  \"q-deformed quantity\" (parameterised by q ≥ 1) to its\n  classical limit;\n* the standard-part identification `cl_via_stpart` showing\n  that `cl_value(q)` equals the standard part of the surreal\n  evaluation at `q = 1 + ε` (here represented as a real\n  function for the formal Lean shell).\n\nA concrete instance discharges `cl_via_stpart_holds` with\n`sorry` (the conjecture); downstream theorems condition on it. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:classical-limit-stpart","label":"conj:classical-limit-stpart","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/classical-limit-stpart.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.StandardPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.StandardPart","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/ClassicalLimitStpart.lean#L29-L31","doc":"Surrogate for the surreal-number standard part: a function\nextracting the real component of a hyperreal/surreal value. ","signatureChunk":0}]}